    "claim": "Crizotinib is a small-molecule, ATP-competitive tyrosine kinase inhibitor that specifically binds to the kinase domain of the ALK protein.",
    "verdict": "HALLUCINATED",
    "rationale": "The provided PubMed context does not describe the biochemical mechanism of action (ATP-competitive inhibition or binding site) of crizotinib."
  },
  {
    "claim": "Crizotinib blocks ALK autophosphorylation and downstream signal transduction.",
    "verdict": "HALLUCINATED",
    "rationale": "The provided PubMed context does not describe the biochemical mechanism of action of crizotinib."
  },
  {
    "claim": "In ALK-positive NSCLC, oncogenic chromosomal rearrangements (such as EML4-ALK) lead to constitutive activation of the ALK kinase.",
    "verdict": "HALLUCINATED",
    "rationale": "The provided PubMed context mentions ALK-positive NSCLC but does not explain the molecular pathology of EML4-ALK rearrangements or constitutive activation."
  },
  {
    "claim": "Constitutive activation of ALK drives hyperactive cell proliferation and anti-apoptotic signaling via pathways like MAPK/ERK and PI3K/AKT.",
    "verdict": "HALLUCINATED",
    "rationale": "The provided PubMed context does not discuss downstream signaling pathways such as MAPK/ERK or PI3K/AKT."
  },
  {
    "claim": "Crizotinib suppresses tumor growth and induces apoptosis in ALK-driven malignant cells.",
    "verdict": "HALLUCINATED",
    "rationale": "The provided PubMed context does not describe the cellular effects (apoptosis/growth suppression) of crizotinib."
  },
  {
    "claim": "The median progression-free survival (PFS) for crizotinib in treatment-naive ALK-positive NSCLC is 12.0 months.",
    "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
    "rationale": "The first PubMed abstract explicitly states: 'Envonalkib significantly improved PFS over crizotinib (median PFS: 30.4 vs. 12.0 months...)'."
  },
